{
  "raw": {
    "https://www.hendrix.edu/humanresources/jobs.aspx?gnk=job&gni=8a78839e9eb34c42019edb8269066e87&lang=en": {
      "title": "Associate Director of Admission- Enrollment Systems",
      "description": "Position: Associate Director of Admission- Enrollment Systems Location: Conway, AR Job Id: 2026,Adm-AssocDirEnroll # of Openings: 1 Associate Director of Admission- Enrollment Systems Hendrix College is seeking a full-time, 12-month Associate Director of Admission- Enrollment Systems. The Associate Director of Admission - Enrollment Systems serves as the primary administrator and strategic steward of Slate CRM for the Office of Admission. This role is responsible for maintaining data integrity, optimizing Slate functionality, supporting recruitment and enrollment workflows, and ensuring that Slate effectively supports a personalized, student-centered admission experience consistent with the mission of a small residential liberal arts college. Reporting directly to the Vice President for Enrollment and operating as a part of the enrollment leadership team, this position blends technical expertise, process design, and collaborative problem-solving. The Associate Director will work closely with admission counselors, financial aid, marketing/communications, and IT. The ideal candidate is detail-oriented and comfortable translating enrollment goals into efficient, reliable Slate solutions. This role will oversee one Administrative Assistant that co-reports to the AVP for Enrollment. Key Responsibilities: Slate Administration & System Ownership Serve as the primary Slate administrator (“Slate Captain”) for Admission Configure, maintain, and document Slate forms, workflows, queries, rules, portals, and events Manage Slate permissions, user roles, and training documentation Monitor Slate releases and updates; recommend and implement enhancements Serve as the primary point of contact for Slate support and vendor communication Data Integrity & Reporting Maintain high standards of data accuracy, consistency, and compliance Develop and manage queries, reports, and dashboards to support recruitment strategy and leadership decision-making Support census, funnel reporting, and enrollment forecasting Partner with Institutional Research and IT to ensure data alignment across systems (Jenzabar, PowerFaids, etc.) Recruitment & Operations Support Support admission counselors with Slate tools for territory management, travel, communication, and applicant review Build and manage communication populations and deliverables (emails, texts, portals, events and assist with visit programming and event registration workflows in Slate, in collaboration with the Assistant Director of Admission- Events and Communications Support application reading processes, decision release workflows, and deposit management Cross-Functional Collaboration Oversee the work of the Administrative Assistant for Financial Aid and Enrollment Systems, ensuring close collaboration between the offices of admission and financial aid and supervising partnerships with vendors on integrations, imports/exports, and system troubleshooting Translate operational needs into scalable Slate solutions Training & Documentation Provide onboarding and ongoing Slate training for admission staff and other campus users of Slate Develop and maintain clear process documentation and user guides Serve as a patient, service-oriented problem solver for Slate users Other duties as assigned Qualifications: Required: Bachelor’s degree Minimum of 3-5 years Slate management experience Experience in higher education admission, enrollment management, or related field Strong analytical skills with demonstrated experience building queries and reports High attention to detail and commitment to data integrity Must be a self-starter and possess a can-do attitude A valid driver's license is required Work Environment: Preference given to candidates living in or willing to relocate to Conway, AR. Remote work will be considered for the right candidate. This role is located in an office setting on the Hendrix College campus. Occasional evening or weekend work may be required during key periods. Consideration of applicants will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Applications should include a letter of application and a resume with contact information for three professional references. The annual salary for this position is commensurate with education and experience. Applications can be submitted at www.hendrix.edu/jobs. Questions about this position can be submitted to hr@hendrix.edu. Hendrix College strives to maintain an environment free from discrimination and harassment, where members of the Hendrix Community treat each other with respect, dignity and courtesy. The College adheres to the principle of equal educational and employment opportunity without regard to age, race, color, religion, gender, disability, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, genetic information, or national origin. Apply for this Position Apply with Indeed Go back to the job list powered by"
    },
    "https://www.hendrix.edu/humanresources/jobs.aspx?gnk=job&gni=8a7887ac9f8b9449019fccc92cc73c06&lang=en": {
      "title": "Director of Digital Strategy",
      "description": "Position: Director of Digital Strategy Location: Conway, AR Job Id: 2026-Comm-DigStr # of Openings: 1 Director of Digital Strategy Hendrix College is seeking a full-time, 12-month Director of Digital Strategy. Reporting to the Chief Communications Officer, the Director of Digital Strategy leads the creation and execution of strategic content across all online platforms, ensuring the College’s digital presence is compelling, cohesive, and aligned with institutional priorities. This role serves as the architect and driver of digital storytelling, overseeing the planning, coordination, and production of written, visual, and multimedia content that supports enrollment, advancement, and brand visibility. In addition to leading content strategy and production, this individual serves as the primary manager for the institution’s website, ensuring it remains dynamic, user-centered, and enrollment-focused. The Director will also shape and strengthen the College’s social media platforms by auditing and repurposing existing content and through the creation of new strategic content designed to maximize engagement and impact. The Director of Digital Strategy is both visionary and hands-on, a multifaceted creative leader who moves quickly, collaborates deeply, and executes with excellence. Exceptional writing, video, photography, and editing skills are essential, along with the ability to translate broad institutional goals into actionable plans and measurable digital outcomes. The successful candidate is comfortable receiving a strategic objective, determining the best path forward, and independently moving work from concept through execution while proactively communicating progress, questions, and recommendations with appropriate stakeholders. This position is well suited for a self-directed professional who enjoys building systems, identifying opportunities, solving problems, and helping shape the future of the College’s digital strategy. Priorities may shift quickly based on institutional needs, and the successful candidate must be comfortable exercising sound judgment, asking timely questions, adapting to changing circumstances, and moving work forward with minimal day-to-day direction. We are a fast-moving, high-performing team. We are looking for someone who brings energy, creativity, discipline, and ownership to everything they do. Desired Attributes Clear, concise, accurate written communication. Intellectual curiosity. Eager to try new ways of working and learn from success and failure—a continuous improvement mindset. Shares and receives ideas without fear or pride of authorship. A team player—honest, thoughtful, direct but kind, and willing to contribute to projects that are not within the job description. Values the residential liberal arts experience and our mission but understands we will have to adapt. Demonstrates initiative by identifying needs, proposing solutions, and advancing work without waiting for detailed instruction. Comfortable translating broad strategic direction into organized plans, priorities, and deliverables. Proactively communicates questions, obstacles, and progress to keep projects moving. Demonstrates sound professional judgment and adapts digital communications appropriately as institutional priorities or circumstances change. Builds strong, trusting relationships across campus and recognizes that effective collaboration is foundational to successful communications. Primary Responsibilities Lead the strategic planning, execution, and continuous improvement of the College's digital presence across all online platforms. Plan, coordinate, and produce high-quality written, photographic, video, and multimedia content. Develop and maintain integrated digital content calendars aligned with recruitment, advancement, and institutional initiatives. Serve as primary manager and strategic lead for the College website (hosted on the WordPress platform), ensuring content quality, optimization, performance, and alignment with institutional goals. Partner with the Communications Specialist to audit, repurpose, and enhance social media platforms for greater effectiveness and engagement. Support media-driven storytelling initiatives in collaboration with the Director of Communications, preparing and amplifying digital content tied to local and regional media coverage. Monitor analytics and performance metrics to refine content strategy and maximize impact. Maintain consistency in brand voice, visual identity, and messaging across all digital platforms. Translate institutional priorities into actionable digital strategies, project plans, timelines, and deliverables. Monitor the College's digital presence, audience engagement, and online conversations to identify emerging opportunities, trends, and reputational issues, making recommendations and adjusting strategy as appropriate. Develop systems, workflows, and processes that improve the efficiency, consistency, and effectiveness of the College's digital communications. Required Qualifications Bachelor’s degree in communications, marketing, journalism, digital media, or related field. 3-5 years of professional experience in digital content strategy, communications, marketing, or a related role. Exceptional writing and storytelling skills with the ability to translate complex ideas into clear, engaging digital content. Demonstrated experience producing and managing multimedia content including video, photography, and written storytelling. Experience managing website content within a CMS environment. WordPress experience preferred. Familiarity with social media strategy, content planning, and audience engagement across multiple platforms. Strong organizational and project management skills with the ability to manage multiple priorities and deadlines simultaneously. Demonstrated ability to independently organize work, establish priorities, and carry projects from concept through completion. Ability to thrive in a collaborative, fast-paced environment where priorities evolve and projects often begin with strategic direction rather than detailed instructions. Excellent judgment, problem-solving ability, and willingness to seek clarification when needed while maintaining ownership of assigned work. Ability to interpret analytics and apply insights to improve digital engagement and performance. A collaborative, solutions-oriented mindset with the ability to work effectively across departments. Consideration of applicants will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Applications should include a letter of application, a resume and contact information for three professional references. Salary is commensurate with education and experience. Applications can be submitted at www.hendrix.edu/jobs. Questions about this position can be submitted to hr@hendrix.edu. Hendrix College strives to maintain an environment free from discrimination and harassment, where members of the Hendrix Community treat each other with respect, dignity and courtesy. The College adheres to the principle of equal educational and employment opportunity without regard to age, race, color, religion, gender, disability, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, genetic information, or national origin. Apply for this Position Apply with Indeed Go back to the job list powered by"
    },
    "https://www.hendrix.edu/humanresources/jobs.aspx?gnk=job&gni=8a78859e9de070f7019e1cdb2d401a10&lang=en": {
      "title": "Custodian",
      "description": "Position: Custodian Location: Conway, AR Job Id: 2026-FM-Cust # of Openings: 1 Custodian Hendrix College is seeking a full-time, support staff Custodian. Working under the direct supervision of the Custodial Supervisor, the Custodian p rovides routine cleaning of buildings, furniture and equipment on a daily basis and conducts routine housekeeping tasks in accordance with established standards and instruction. JOB DUTIES & RESPONSIBILITIES: Sweep, mop and scrub floors, stairs (inside and outside buildings) and other surfaces. Must keep all dispensers appropriately filled. Use light and heavy (industrial type) floor machines and attachments. Scrub, strip and wax floors using heavy (industrial type) powered scrubber and buffers. Vacuum rugs/carpets in offices and public areas. Shampoo rugs/carpets periodically using heavy vacuum cleaner and rug shampooing machine. Clean and dust furniture, exhibit cases, pictures, door trim and chalkboards. Clean, equipment and scrubbers and change brushes, pads, rollers, buffers and other attachments. Wash window sills, glass in corridor doors, and clean blinds. Wash and/or clean interior wall s paces while working on ladders. Clean and service lavatories, toilet rooms and restrooms. Collect trash and debris and place in collection area for removal by Facilities personnel. Replace liners in wastebaskets and trash containers. Move heavy furniture, supplies and miscellaneous equipment, as directed. Submit workorders for needed repairs (doors, door checks, furniture lights, faucets, etc.). Must adhere to all safety standards and work practices established by Facilities Management. Perform a number of special projects related to various aspects of Facilities Management. Complete and/or maintain department records and forms relating to the custodial operation. Conduct routine building inspections to assess needs. Performs specialized tasks during adverse weather conditions and college closures. In the event of unscheduled closures due to weather events and/or other circumstances, serves as “essential personnel” for reopening the college. Must complete all required training as scheduled. Perform other duties, as assigned. ESSENTIAL SKILLS: Must have a high school diploma or equivalent. Ability to read, write and follow oral and written instructions. Ability to bend, stoop, climb ladders, move and/or push/pull equipment. Must be able to lift a minimum of 50 pounds. Must be dependable, punctual and have a good attendance record. Must be able to work overtime and/or weekends, when required. Consideration of applicants will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Applications should include a resume and contact information for three professional references. Salary is $12.00 per hour. Applications can be submitted at www.hendrix.edu/jobs. Questions about this position can be submitted to hr@hendrix.edu. Hendrix College strives to maintain an environment free from discrimination and harassment, where members of the Hendrix Community treat each other with respect, dignity and courtesy. The College adheres to the principle of equal educational and employment opportunity without regard to age, race, color, religion, gender, disability, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, genetic information, or national origin. Apply for this Position Apply with Indeed Go back to the job list powered by"
    },
    "https://www.hendrix.edu/humanresources/jobs.aspx?gnk=job&gni=8a7883ac9d02ffb2019d203a127750ca&lang=en": {
      "title": "Adjunct Instructor of Physics",
      "description": "Position: Adjunct Instructor of Physics Location: Conway, AR Job Id: 2026-Physics-Adj # of Openings: 1 Adjunct Instructor of Physics The Department of Physics at Hendrix College seeks applications for an Adjunct Instructor of Physics to teach one section of PHYS 160: Astronomy – an introductory survey course intended for non-science majors, for either semester of the 2026-2027 academic year. The instruction of this course takes place on campus and typically meets for three one-hour sessions per week. Instructors are also expected to provide reasonable office hours to support student learning. Applications will be reviewed until the position is filled. A master’s degree or higher is required. Applications for the position should include a letter addressing the candidate’s interest in teaching in a liberal arts environment, a curriculum vitae/resume, transcripts (unofficial) from highest degree earned, and list of three references including email address and phone number. Please email any questions to Dr. Julie Gunderson ( gundersonj@hendrix.edu ), Chair of the Physics Department. Hendrix is a distinguished liberal arts college located in Conway, Arkansas, thirty miles from Little Rock at the foothills of the Ozark Mountains. The College, affiliated with the United Methodist Church, has a strong commitment to excellence in teaching liberal arts. Hendrix College strives to maintain an environment free from discrimination and harassment, where employees treat each other with respect, dignity, and courtesy. The College adheres to the principle of equal educational and employment opportunity without regard to age, race, color, religion, gender, disability, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, genetic information, or national origin. Apply for this Position Apply with Indeed Go back to the job list powered by"
    },
    "https://www.hendrix.edu/humanresources/jobs.aspx?gnk=job&gni=8a7885a89e235a1d019e40593a8e15a2&lang=en": {
      "title": "Adjunct Instructor of Spanish",
      "description": "Position: Adjunct Instructor of Spanish Location: Conway, AR Job Id: 2026-ForLang-Spanish # of Openings: 1 Adjunct Instructor of Spanish The Department of Languages at Hendrix College seeks applications for an Adjunct Instructor of Spanish to teach one section of SPAN 110: Fundamentals of Spanish I in the fall semester and one section of SPAN 120: Fundamentals of Spanish II in the spring semester. The instruction of these courses takes place on campus and will meet for four one-hour sessions per week. Instructors are also expected to provide reasonable office hours to support student learning. Applications will be reviewed until the position is filled. A master’s or higher in Spanish is required. Applications for the position should include a letter addressing the candidate’s interest in teaching in a liberal arts environment, a curriculum vitae/resume, transcripts (unofficial) from highest degree earned, and list of three references including email address and phone number. Please email any questions to Dr. Lilian Contreras-Silva (contreras@hendrix.edu), Coordinator of the Spanish Program. Hendrix is a distinguished liberal arts college located in Conway, Arkansas, thirty miles from Little Rock at the foothills of the Ozark Mountains. The College, affiliated with the United Methodist Church, has a strong commitment to excellence in teaching liberal arts. Hendrix College strives to maintain an environment free from discrimination and harassment, where employees treat each other with respect, dignity, and courtesy. The College adheres to the principle of equal educational and employment opportunity without regard to age, race, color, religion, gender, disability, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, genetic information, or national origin. Apply for this Position Apply with Indeed Go back to the job list powered by"
    },
    "https://www.hendrix.edu/humanresources/jobs.aspx?gnk=job&gni=8a78859ea133541101a1358052c420ab&lang=en": {
      "title": "Assistant or Associate Professor of Economics and Business - Management (2 positions)",
      "description": "Position: Assistant or Associate Professor of Economics and Business - Management (2 positions) Location: Conway, AR Job Id: 106-Mgmt # of Openings: 1 Assistant or Associate Professor of Economics and Business - Management (2 positions) Hendrix College invites applications for two tenure-track positions at the rank of assistant or associate professor of economics and business specializing in management to begin in August 2027. The successful candidates will work with other Economics and Business faculty to launch a new Business management major which is anticipated to start in August 2027. While we welcome candidates with broad interests in the management field, candidates with interests in sports, healthcare, operations, or supply chain management are particularly encouraged to apply. Primary teaching duties will include introductory and upper-level Business Management courses such as Principles of Management, Organization Behavior, Business Communications, Business Ethics, and upper-level Business Management electives. The normal teaching load is three courses per semester. The terminal degree requirement is a Ph.D. in Business Management or a related field such as Business Administration or Business Analytics; ABD will be considered. Celebrated among the country’s leading liberal arts colleges for academic quality, engaged learning opportunities and career preparation, vibrant campus life, and value, Hendrix has been named one of the nation’s Most Innovative Schools in the latest U.S. News & World Report Best Colleges rankings and is featured in Colleges That Change Lives: 45 Schools That Will Change the Way You Think About Colleges. The College seeks to extend its tradition of excellence in teaching and scholarship by attracting faculty who combine mastery of their disciplines with broad intellectual interests and commitment to the aims of a liberal arts college. Candidates who are excited to contribute to our new Via Hendrix curriculum , which combines hands-on work experience with a strong liberal arts education, are particularly encouraged to apply. Applications should include a cover letter addressing the candidate’s interest in teaching in a liberal arts environment, a curriculum vitae, a statement of teaching and scholarly interests, evidence of teaching effectiveness, and graduate and undergraduate transcripts (unofficial are acceptable at this stage). In addition, three letters of recommendation should be requested and sent by e-mail to FacultyRecs@hendrix.edu . Applications can be submitted at www.hendrix.edu/jobs . Review of materials will begin October 26, 2026 and will continue until the position is filled. Please direct questions to Gina Bergfeld at bergfeld@hendrix.edu , particularly if you are interested in more information about the position in advance of applying. Hendrix is a distinguished liberal arts college located in Conway, Arkansas, thirty miles from Little Rock at the foothills of the Ozark Mountains. The College, affiliated with the United Methodist Church, has a strong commitment to excellence in teaching liberal arts and career preparation. Hendrix College is an equal opportunity employer, and all applications will be considered without regard to race, gender, disability, sexual orientation, national origin or any other characteristic specified by law. The College is committed to maintaining an atmosphere of civility and respect for all students, faculty, and staff. Apply for this Position Apply with Indeed Go back to the job list powered by"
    },
    "https://www.hendrix.edu/humanresources/jobs.aspx?gnk=job&gni=8a78859ea133541101a1358b099324bd&lang=en": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Chemistry (Pharmaceutical Sciences)",
      "description": "Position: Assistant Professor of Chemistry (Pharmaceutical Sciences) Location: Conway, AR Job Id: 107-Chem # of Openings: 1 Assistant Professor of Chemistry (Pharmaceutical Sciences) Hendrix College invites applications for a tenure-track position as an assistant professor of chemistry in the area of pharmaceutical chemistry to begin in August 2027. The successful candidate will work with other natural science faculty to launch a new Pharmaceutical Sciences major which is anticipated to start in August 2027. They will teach courses in pharmacology and toxicology, medicinal chemistry, and drug discovery and development and also be expected to contribute to the organic chemistry or biochemistry sequence of courses, depending on their area of expertise. The position comes with competitive start-up funding and carries a full-time teaching load of six course equivalents per year, where one course equivalent comprises a lecture section or two lab sections. Doctorate at time of appointment is required, postdoctoral experience is preferred. Celebrated among the country’s leading liberal arts colleges for academic quality, engaged learning opportunities and career preparation, vibrant campus life, and value, Hendrix has been named one of the nation’s Most Innovative Schools in the latest U.S. News & World Report Best Colleges rankings and is featured in Colleges That Change Lives: 45 Schools That Will Change the Way You Think About Colleges. The College seeks to extend its tradition of excellence in teaching and scholarship by attracting faculty who combine mastery of their disciplines with broad intellectual interests and commitment to the aims of a liberal arts college. Candidates who are excited to contribute to our new Via Hendrix curriculum , which combines hands-on work experience with a strong liberal arts education, are encouraged to apply. Applications should include a cover letter addressing the candidate’s interest in teaching in a liberal arts environment, a curriculum vitae, a statement of teaching and research interests, evidence of teaching effectiveness, and graduate and undergraduate transcripts (unofficial are acceptable at this stage). In addition, three letters of recommendation should be requested and sent by e-mail to FacultyRecs@hendrix.edu . Applications can be submitted at www.hendrix.edu/jobs . Review of materials will begin November 1, 2026 and will continue until the position is filled. Please direct questions to Chemistry Department Chair Dr. Peter Kett at kett@hendrix.edu , especially if you are interested in more information about the position in advance of applying. Hendrix is a distinguished liberal arts college located in Conway, Arkansas, thirty miles from Little Rock at the foothills of the Ozark Mountains. The College, affiliated with the United Methodist Church, has a strong commitment to excellence in teaching liberal arts and career preparation. Hendrix College is an equal opportunity employer, and all applications will be considered without regard to race, gender, disability, sexual orientation, national origin or any other characteristic specified by law. The College is committed to maintaining an atmosphere of civility and respect for all students, faculty, and staff. Apply for this Position Apply with Indeed Go back to the job list powered by"
    },
    "https://www.hendrix.edu/humanresources/jobs.aspx?gnk=job&gni=8a78859ea133541101a13578e7581db4&lang=en": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Economics and Business – Economics",
      "description": "Position: Assistant Professor of Economics and Business – Economics Location: Conway, AR Job Id: 105-Econ # of Openings: 1 Assistant Professor of Economics and Business – Economics Hendrix College invites applications for a tenure-track position as an assistant professor of economics and business in the area of economics to begin in August 2027. While we welcome candidates with broad interests in the field of economics, candidates with interests in health, environmental, or behavioral economics are particularly encouraged to apply. Primary teaching duties will include introductory and upper-level economics courses such as microeconomics, macroeconomics, statistics, econometrics, economic research, and upper-level economics electives. The normal teaching load is three courses per semester. The terminal degree requirement is a Ph.D. in Economics; ABD will be considered. Celebrated among the country’s leading liberal arts colleges for academic quality, engaged learning opportunities and career preparation, vibrant campus life, and value, Hendrix has been named one of the nation’s Most Innovative Schools in the latest U.S. News & World Report Best Colleges rankings and is featured in Colleges That Change Lives: 45 Schools That Will Change the Way You Think About Colleges. The College seeks to extend its tradition of excellence in teaching and scholarship by attracting faculty who combine mastery of their disciplines with broad intellectual interests and commitment to the aims of a liberal arts college. Candidates who are excited to contribute to our new Via Hendrix curriculum , which combines hands-on work experience with a strong liberal arts education, are particularly encouraged to apply. Applications should include a cover letter addressing the candidate’s interest in teaching in a liberal arts environment, a curriculum vitae, a statement of teaching interests, evidence of teaching effectiveness, and graduate and undergraduate transcripts (unofficial transcripts are acceptable at this stage). In addition, three letters of recommendation should be requested and sent by e-mail to FacultyRecs@hendrix.edu . Applications can be submitted at www.hendrix.edu/jobs . Review of materials will begin October 26, 2026 and will continue until the position is filled. Please direct questions to Gina Bergfeld at bergfeld@hendrix.edu , particularly if you are interested in more information about the position in advance of applying. Hendrix is a distinguished liberal arts college located in Conway, Arkansas, thirty miles from Little Rock at the foothills of the Ozark Mountains. The College, affiliated with the United Methodist Church, has a strong commitment to excellence in teaching liberal arts and career preparation. Hendrix College is an equal opportunity employer, and all applications will be considered without regard to race, gender, disability, sexual orientation, national origin or any other characteristic specified by law. The College is committed to maintaining an atmosphere of civility and respect for all students, faculty, and staff. Apply for this Position Apply with Indeed Go back to the job list powered by"
    },
    "https://www.hendrix.edu/humanresources/jobs.aspx?gnk=job&gni=8a78879ea15447f701a163dddbb462a7&lang=en": {
      "title": "Mover",
      "description": "Position: Mover Location: Conway, AR Job Id: 110-Mover # of Openings: 1 Mover Hendrix College is seeking a full-time, support staff Mover. Working under the direct supervision of the Moving Supervisor, the Mover p erforms all aspects of moving requests including set-ups, take-downs, and preparation for special events. Directs the work of Movers or other assigned employees. JOB DUTIES & RESPONSIBILITIES: Perform general moving duties and assist other departments when needed. Works closely with requestors and coordinate the movers to ensure adequate coverage for special events in a timely manner. Complete moving/set-up/breakdown work orders and delivery of freight. Operates moving vehicle in conjunction with delivery of freight and performance of moving work order duties. Communicate positively with faculty, staff, and students in completion of duties. Do routine care of all moving vehicles. Deliver housekeeping supplies. Maintains and sets all student room furniture as needed. Assists with all furniture moving on campus. Deliver heavy mail packages and freight deliveries. Maintain a clean and orderly warehouse. Ensure workorders are completed in a timely manner in SchoolDude. Performs specialized tasks during adverse weather conditions and college closures. In the event of unscheduled closures due to weather events and/or other circumstances, serves as “essential personnel” for reopening the college. Must complete all required training as scheduled. Other duties as assigned. ESSENTIAL SKILLS: Ability to read, write and follow oral and written instructions. High School diploma or equivalent. Walking, stooping and climbing for long periods of time. Lifting of objects weighing more than 50 pounds. Ability to withstand extreme hot/cold weather. Operation of heavy equipment. Ability to work safely with hazardous chemicals in a cautious and safe manner. Ability to work overtime and/or weekends. Must be dependable, punctual and have a good attendance record. Must have current Arkansas drivers license. The Facilities Department will contact individuals for interviews based on applications submitted through this page. Due to the volume of applications and interest that we receive, we do ask that you refrain from calling our Facilities Department directly. Consideration of applicants will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Applications can be submitted at www.hendrix.edu/jobs. Questions about this position can be submitted to hr@hendrix.edu. . Hendrix College strives to maintain an environment free from discrimination and harassment, where members of the Hendrix Community treat each other with respect, dignity and courtesy. The College adheres to the principle of equal educational and employment opportunity without regard to age, race, color, religion, gender, disability, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, genetic information, or national origin. Apply for this Position Apply with Indeed Go back to the job list powered by"
    },
    "https://www.hendrix.edu/humanresources/jobs.aspx?gnk=job&gni=8a78859fa152cc4201a15f59e21a79a4&lang=en": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Art",
      "description": "Position: Assistant Professor of Art Location: Conway, AR Job Id: 109-Art # of Openings: 1 Assistant Professor of Art Hendrix College invites applications for a tenure-track position as an assistant professor of art with an emphasis in 3D art to begin in August 2027. The successful candidate will teach courses in ceramics and 3D art such as wheel throwing, sculpture, 3D design, and mixed media; supervise studio activities, including oversight of kiln operations, studio maintenance, and health and safety protocols; and engage in their professional studio work. Our facilities are excellent with spaces for a variety of studio art disciplines. We are well equipped to support 3D art including a comprehensive ceramics and sculpture studio, foundry area, woodshop, and 3D printers. An MFA in Art or a related field (or equivalent professional experience) is required by the start date; candidates who are ABD at the time of application will be considered. Celebrated among the country’s leading liberal arts colleges for academic quality, engaged learning opportunities and career preparation, vibrant campus life, and value, Hendrix has been named one of the nation’s Most Innovative Schools in the latest U.S. News & World Report Best Colleges rankings and is featured in Colleges That Change Lives: 45 Schools That Will Change the Way You Think About Colleges. The College seeks to extend its tradition of excellence in teaching and scholarship by attracting faculty who combine mastery of their disciplines with broad intellectual interests and commitment to the aims of a liberal arts college. Candidates who are excited to contribute to our new Via Hendrix curriculum , which combines hands-on work experience with a strong liberal arts education, are encouraged to apply. Applications should include a cover letter addressing the candidate’s interest in teaching in a liberal arts environment, a curriculum vitae that includes information about exhibitions and prior teaching experience, a statement of teaching interests, evidence of teaching effectiveness, and graduate and undergraduate transcripts (unofficial transcripts are acceptable at this stage). If unable to upload transcripts as one document, you may email one or both of them to facultyrecs@hendrix.edu. The cover letter should also include a link to an outline portfolio of 15-20 images of your recent work and a link to an online portfolio of no more than 20 images of student work (if available). In addition, three letters of recommendation should be requested and sent by e-mail to FacultyRecs@hendrix.edu . Applications can be submitted at www.hendrix.edu/jobs . Review of materials will begin November 1, 2026 and will continue until the position is filled. Please direct questions to Art Department Chair Dr. Rod Miller at miller@hendrix.edu , particularly if you are interested in more information about the position in advance of applying. Hendrix is a distinguished liberal arts college located in Conway, Arkansas, thirty miles from Little Rock at the foothills of the Ozark Mountains. The College, affiliated with the United Methodist Church, has a strong commitment to excellence in teaching liberal arts and career preparation. Hendrix College is an equal opportunity employer, and all applications will be considered without regard to race, gender, disability, sexual orientation, national origin or any other characteristic specified by law. The College is committed to maintaining an atmosphere of civility and respect for all students, faculty, and staff. Apply for this Position Apply with Indeed Go back to the job list powered by"
    },
    "https://www.hendrix.edu/humanresources/jobs.aspx?gnk=job&gni=8a78859fa152cc4201a15f01b2054ea7&lang=en": {
      "title": "Part-Time Public Safety Officer",
      "description": "Position: Part-Time Public Safety Officer Location: Conway, AR Job Id: 108-PSO # of Openings: 1 Public Safety Officer (Part-Time) Hendrix College is seeking a part-time, 12-month support staff position. Reporting to the Director of Public Safety, the Public Safety Officer ensures the safety of persons and property on the Hendrix campus and helps manage various emergency situations. POSITION RESPONSIBILITIES: Patrol campus buildings and grounds to prevent or respond to conduct that is a violation of law and/or College expectations to include incidents of theft, vandalism, fire or fire hazards, disorderly conduct, parking violations, etc. Ensure buildings are locked and unlocked as appropriate. Inspect life safety equipment, which includes checking locks, lighting, fire extinguishers and alarms to confirm they are in working order. Report any public safety incidents and unusual or hazardous conditions on campus to appropriate officials (i.e., inoperative alarms, discharged or defective fire extinguishers, broken windows, etc.). Investigate complaints made by faculty, staff, or students on campus. Investigate traffic accidents on campus. Assist local law enforcement, fire, and other emergency personnel as needed. Foster lasting relationships and trust with students, staff, and faculty through open and effective communication. Provide public safety services such as parking and traffic direction, crowd control, and the like, for special events. Issue parking citations and report traffic violations. Assist police with investigations on campus. Provide visitors directions and general Hendrix College information. Complete all required paperwork on campus incidents and public safety activities. Perform other duties as assigned by the Director of Public Safety. POSITION QUALIFICATIONS: Looking for friendly, motivated, enthusiastic candidates. Education and Experience: High school diploma or equivalent plus experience in customer service. Knowledge of first aid techniques; CPR certification is a plus. Experience working as a member of a team and building relationships with those you serve and support. In-House training provided. Required Skills: Familiarity with relevant laws; basic knowledge of fire prevention; valid driver’s license; ability to deal effectively with a wide range of individuals, in some instances under stressful, dangerous and/or emergency conditions; ability to handle emergency situations calmly and efficiently; demonstrated integrity; must have the physical ability to perform all job duties. Writing skills that allow for comprehensive reporting of incident response and engagement with members of the College community. Consideration of applicants will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Applications should include a resume with contact information for three professional references. Salary is commensurate with education and experience. Applications can be submitted at www.hendrix.edu/jobs. Questions about this position can be submitted to hr@hendrix.edu. Hendrix College strives to maintain an environment free from discrimination and harassment, where members of the Hendrix Community treat each other with respect, dignity and courtesy. The College adheres to the principle of equal educational and employment opportunity without regard to age, race, color, religion, gender, disability, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, genetic information, or national origin. You can learn more about the College's commitment to diversity and inclusion by reviewing our statement: https://www.hendrix.edu/diversity/statement/. Apply for this Position Apply with Indeed Go back to the job list powered by"
    }
  },
